CAUGHT DEFECT (fixed): the vendored src/.gitignore ships patterns meant
for tinycc's OWN working tree (build artifacts) but two of them also
matched real upstream files, so a plain `git add` silently dropped them.
Audited by diffing `git ls-files` in a fresh upstream checkout of the
pinned commit against the committed third-party/tcc/src tree:
  - src/conftest.c  — matched src/.gitignore's `conftest*` pattern, but
    IS a real upstream source file: configure's compiler probe compiles
    it, and the top-level Makefile compiles it with -DC2STR to build
    c2str.exe (needed to generate tccdefs_.h). REQUIRED — force-added
    with `git add -f` (see the commit that added this note).
  - src/win32/include/tcc/tcc_libm.h — matched src/.gitignore's
    `win32/include/tcc/tccdefs.h`-adjacent win32 exclusions (this whole
    win32/include/tcc/ subtree is win32-only). Confirmed NOT needed: only
    referenced from win32/include/math.h (`#include "tcc/tcc_libm.h"`),
    which is itself excluded and irrelevant to our native Linux aarch64
    build. Left excluded — this is a correct, audited omission, not an
    oversight.
No other upstream files were found excluded (full `git ls-files` diff
against the pinned commit shows exactly these two after the conftest.c
fix, and only the second is intentional).

